<GuideLayout 
  title="How to Choose a Private Label Activewear Manufacturer"
  description="A comprehensive guide for B2B brands on auditing factories, verifying certifications, and ensuring quality consistency in activewear production."
  publishDate="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>Selecting the right manufacturing partner is the most critical decision for any activewear brand. A mismatch here can lead to inconsistent sizing, poor fabric quality, and missed launch dates. Here is the Fitclo blueprint for auditing a potential private label partner.</p>

  <h2>1. Verify the 'Real' Factory Status</h2>
  <p>Many 'manufacturers' are actually trading companies. While they have their place, a direct B2B partnership requires factory transparency. Look for proof of scale—for example, Fitclo’s 16,000㎡ production facility is fully owned and operated, which allows us to control the QC process from yarn to finished garment.</p>

  <h2>2. Check for Specialized Machinery</h2>
  <p>Activewear requires specific tech: 4-needle 6-thread (flatlock) machines, laser cutters for seamless edges, and specialized heat-press stations for reflective logos. Ask for a virtual factory tour or raw production videos to see these machines in action on your specific product category.</p>

  <h2>3. Lead Time and MOQ Scalability</h2>
  <p>A great partner grows with you. Can they handle a Low MOQ of 50 pieces for your market testing phase? And more importantly, can they scale to 50,000 pieces when you hit a viral trend? Scalability in manufacturing is about having the floor space and the workforce to shift priorities instantly.</p>

</GuideLayout>
